---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Introduction" activeNav="/">
  <h1>App Manager Platform</h1>
  <p>
    A multi-tenant mobile app management platform with a REST API for managing
    applications, builds, credentials, CI/CD pipelines, Expo integration, and outbound webhooks.
  </p>

  <h2>Quick links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/getting-started">Getting Started</a> — set up your first API key and make your first request</li>
    <li><a href="/cli">CLI (appmctl)</a> — install and use the command-line client for CI/CD and automation</li>
    <li><a href="/api-reference">API Reference</a> — interactive documentation with request testing</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/authentication">Authentication</a> — API keys, scopes, and permissions</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Base URL</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="text" code={`http://localhost:8000/api/v1/{team_slug}`} />
  <p>
    All endpoints are scoped to a team via the <code>team_slug</code> path parameter.
    Resources from one team are never exposed to another.
  </p>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>
  <p>Every request requires a Bearer token (API key) and an Accept header:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="http" code={`Authorization: Bearer {api-key}
Accept: application/json`} />
  <p>
    API keys are created in the team settings panel. The plaintext key is shown only once at creation time.
    Each key belongs to exactly one team and is scoped to specific permissions.
  </p>

  <h2>Key concepts</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Concept</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Mobile Apps</strong></td><td>Core entity — a mobile application with metadata, assets, identifiers, and credentials</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>App Identifiers</strong></td><td>Platform-specific identifiers (iOS bundle ID, Android package name, Web domain)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Credentials</strong></td><td>Signing certificates, keystores, provisioning profiles with encrypted payloads</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Builds</strong></td><td>Build records with lifecycle management (manual and automatic modes)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Artifacts</strong></td><td>Build output files (IPA, APK, AAB)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>CI/CD Pipelines</strong></td><td>GitHub Actions and GitLab CI/CD workflow configurations</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Integrations</strong></td><td>External services (GitHub, GitLab, Expo, webhooks)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Webhooks</strong></td><td>Outbound webhook endpoints with HMAC-SHA256 signed deliveries</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Response format</h2>
  <p>All responses use a standard envelope:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="json" code={`{
  "data": { /* resource or array */ },
  "links": { /* pagination links */ },
  "meta": { /* pagination metadata */ }
}`} />

  <h2>HTTP status codes</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>200</code></td><td>Success (read/update)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>201</code></td><td>Created</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>202</code></td><td>Accepted (queued)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>204</code></td><td>No Content (delete)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td>Unauthenticated</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>403</code></td><td>Forbidden</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>404</code></td><td>Not Found (including cross-team access)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>409</code></td><td>Conflict (invalid state transition)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>422</code></td><td>Validation Error</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>502/503</code></td><td>Upstream provider error (Expo)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
